lisa-design:
- Read side uses a separate CurrentRuleset type (embeds Ruleset, shadows BypassActors with *[]BypassActor) instead of changing Ruleset: desired/write rulesets must always send bypass_actors (ccf-required: [], ccf-review: the bot), so the write type keeps a plain slice.
- nil pointer = absent OR null = unknown; pointer to [] = known none. GitHub sends [] for "none" to a write token, so null is not treated as none.
- Unknown bypass is one Plan.Unknown entry per ruleset (key ruleset[<name>].bypass, Current = the existing `unknown` constant, Desired = JSON of the desired bypass view), never a Change; the bypass key is removed from both views before diffing the rest.
- A ruleset with unknown bypass is always scheduled for a full PUT (same idempotent pattern as the merge-settings PATCH); with an otherwise in-sync repo and a read-only token a dry run now shows 9 unknown (7 merge + 2 rulesets).
- Reader.Rulesets now returns map[int64]CurrentRuleset; only reposettings implements/consumes it, so the interface change stays inside the package.
- Test fixture githubDefaults now uses []BypassActor{} (present-and-empty) for the old ccf-review ruleset, matching what a write token reads; nil would now mean hidden.

